REAGENT SETUP   
Collagen stock solution $({\bf600}{\bf\upmu}{\bf g}/{\bf m l})$ Dissolve $15\mathrm{mg}$ of collagen type IV with $25\mathrm{ml}$ of deionized water and $50\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of glacial acidic acid in a beaker. Cover the holding beaker with Parafilm and stir it moderately at room temperature $(22{-}25^{\circ}\mathrm{C})$ until the collagen is dissolved, which takes   
${\sim}15{\mathrm{-}}20~\mathrm{min}$ . Filter-sterilize the solution with a $0.2\mathrm{-}\upmu\mathrm{m}$ -pore filter.   
Prepare $\mathrm{1-ml}$ aliquots and freeze them at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 6 months.   
 CRITICAL It is best to prescreen a lot before buying a large quantity. Lots can vary in terms of potency of cell attachment and possible toxicity to cells.   
Gelatin solution, $0.1\%$ (wt/vol)  Dissolve $100~\mathrm{{mg}}$ of gelatin in $\mathrm{100ml}$ of PBS $(+\mathrm{Ca}^{2+}{+}\mathrm{Mg}^{2+})$ . Filter-sterilize the solution using a $0.22\mathrm{-}\upmu\mathrm{m}$ membrane filter. Store the solution at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 3 months.   
FACS buffer  Dissolve $5\mathrm{g}$ of BSA in $250~\mathrm{ml}$ of PBS. Sterilize the buffer using a Stericup filter $(0.22\upmu\mathrm{m})$ , and store it at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 3 months.   
BSA, $1\%$ (wt/vol) in PBS  Dissolve $_\textrm{1g}$ of BSA in $100\mathrm{ml}$ of PBS. Sterilize the solution by using a $0.22\mathrm{-}\upmu\mathrm{m}$ membrane filter, and store it at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 4 weeks.   
PFA, $4\%$ $\mathbf{(vol/vol)}$ Dilute $10\%$ (vol/vol) PFA in PBS by mixing $20~\mathrm{ml}$ of $10\%$ PFA with $30\mathrm{ml}$ of PBS. This solution can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 2 weeks. ! CAUTION This should be performed in a fume hood.   
PFA, $1\%$ (vol/vol)  Dilute $10\%$ (vol/vol) PFA in PBS by mixing $5\mathrm{ml}$ of $10\%$ PFA with $45~\mathrm{ml}$ of PBS. This solution can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 2 weeks. ! CAUTION This should be performed in a fume hood.
## protocol
$\mathbf{0.25\%}$ (vol/vol) Triton X-100 in PBS  Add $1.25~\mathrm{ml}$ of Triton X-100 to $500\mathrm{ml}$ of PBS. Sterilize the solution by filtrating using a $0.22\mathrm{-}\upmu\mathrm{m}$ membrane filter, and store it at room temperature for up to 1 year.
BMP4 $(25\upmu\mathrm{g}/\mathrm{ml}$ stock solution)  Reconstitute the contents of the vial to a concentration of $25\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ in sterile $4\mathrm{mM}$ HCl containing $0.1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA. Prepare aliquots and store them at $-80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
FGF2 ( $\bf{50}\upmu\mathrm{g}/m l$ stock solution)  Reconstitute the contents of the vial to a concentration of $50\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ in PBS containing $1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA. Prepare aliquots and store them at $-80{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
Activin A $(25\upmu\mathrm{g}/\mathrm{ml}$ stock solution)  Reconstitute the contents of the vial to a concentration of $25\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ in sterile PBS containing $1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA. Prepare aliquots and store them at $-80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
FGF10 $\bf{100}\upmu\bf{g/m l}$ stock solution)  Reconstitute the contents of the vial to a concentration of $100\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ in sterile PBS containing $1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA. Prepare aliquots and store them at $-80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
FGF7 $\bf{\Omega}\cdot\bf{10}\mu\bf{g}/m l$ stock solution)  Reconstitute the contents of the vial to a concentration of $10\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ in sterile PBS containing $1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA. Prepare aliquots and store them at $-80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
FGF18 $(25\upmu\mathrm{g}/\mathrm{ml}$ stock solution)  Reconstitute the contents of the vial to a concentration of $25\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ in sterile PBS containing $1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA. Prepare aliquots and store them at $-80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
SHH $25\upmu\mathrm{g}/\mathrm{ml}$ stock solution)  Reconstitute the contents of the vial to a concentration of $25\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ in sterile distilled water. Prepare aliquots and store them at $-80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
WNT3a $(200~\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ stock solution)  Reconstitute the contents of the vial to a concentration of $200\upmu\mathrm{g/ml}$ in sterile PBS containing $1\%$ (wt/vol) BSA. Prepare aliquots and store them at $-80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
mTESR1  Prepare mTESR medium by mixing $100\mathrm{ml}$ of mTSER1 supplement with $400\mathrm{ml}$ of mTSER1 basal medium. vRITICAL Make sure that the basal medium and supplement end with the same letter (i.e., same lot no.). The medium can be stored at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 2 weeks, or divide the solution into aliquots and store them at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 6 months.
Amiloride $\bf{30m g/m l}$ stock solution)  Dissolve $30~\mathrm{mg}$ of amiloride powder in $1\mathrm{ml}$ of DMSO. Store the solution in aliquots at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
Forskolin $\mathbf{4.1\mg/ml}$ stock solution)  Dissolve $4.1\mathrm{mg}$ of forskolin powder in $\mathrm{1ml}$ of DMSO. Store the solution in aliquots at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
IBMX $(22.2\mathrm{mg/ml}$ stock solution)  Dissolve $22.2\mathrm{mg}$ of IBMX powder in $\mathrm{1~ml}$ of DMSO. Store the solution in aliquots at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year. Genistein $(13.5\mathrm{mg/ml}$ stock solution)  Dissolve $13.5\mathrm{mg}$ of genistein powder in $\mathrm{1ml}$ of DMSO. Store the solution in aliquots at $-20{}^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year. Iodide solution  Dissolve $20.4\ \mathrm{g}$ of sodium iodide, $4.8\mathrm{~g~}$ of HEPES, $2.0\mathrm{g}$ of glucose, $0.5\mathrm{g}$ of calcium nitrate and $0.3\mathrm{\g}$ of potassium nitrate in 1 liter of double deionized water. Adjust the pH to 7.2 with sodium hydroxide.
 CRITICAL Make sure that the osmolarity of the solution is $300\mathrm{mOsm}$ .   
Filter the solution and store it at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.
Nitrate solution  Dissolve $11.6\mathrm{g}$ of sodium nitrate, $4.8\mathrm{~g~}$ of HEPES, $2.0\ \mathrm{g}$ of glucose, $0.5\mathrm{g}$ of calcium nitrate and $0.3\mathrm{\g}$ of potassium nitrate in 1 liter of double deionized water. Adjust the pH to 7.2 with sodium hydroxide.
 CRITICAL Make sure that the osmolarity of the solution is $300\mathrm{mOsm}$ . Filter the solution and store it at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 year.  CRITICAL Before use, add $100\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of stock amiloride solution to $100\mathrm{ml}$ of nitrate solution. cAMP agonist solution  Dissolve $10\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of forskolin stock solution, $10\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of IBMX stock solution and $10\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of genistein stock solution in $10~\mathrm{ml}$ of nitrate solution. Freshly prepare and keep it for no more than 1 h at room temperature.
Lysis buffer  Dissolve $4.0\ \mathrm{g}$ of Tris chloride, $4.4\ \mathrm{g}$ of sodium chloride and $0.15\mathrm{g}$ of EDTA in $500\mathrm{ml}$ of double-deionized water. Adjust the pH to 7.4 and store it at room temperature for up to 1 year.  CRITICAL Before lysis of cells, add $50\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of protease K inhibitor, $100\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of $10\%$ (wt/vol) SDS and $50\upmu\mathrm{l}$ of Triton X-100 to $4.8~\mathrm{ml}$ of lysis buffer.
Laemmli buffer $5\times$ stock solution)  Dissolve $1.9\mathrm{g}$ of Trizma, $5.0\mathrm{g}$ of SDS, $1.0\mathrm{g}$ of DTT and a few drops of bromophenol blue in $25~\mathrm{ml}$ of glycerol; adjust the final volume to $50\mathrm{ml}$ with double deionized water. Store the buffer at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 6 months.
Running buffer  Add $100\mathrm{ml}$ of Tris-glycine-SDS buffer to $900~\mathrm{ml}$ of double deionized water. Store the buffer at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 6 months.
Transfer buffer  Dissolve $14.4~\mathrm{g}$ of glycine and $3.0\mathrm{\g}$ of Tris base in $800~\mathrm{ml}$ of double deionized water. Add $200~\mathrm{ml}$ of methanol to the solution.  CRITICAL Add methanol just before use; do not store this solution for the long term. PBS ( $10\times$ stock solution)  Dissolve $\mathtt{14.2g}$ of sodium phosphate dibasic and $87.7\ \mathrm{g}$ of sodium chloride in 1 liter of double deionized water. Adjust the pH to 7.2 and store it at room temperature for 1 year.
PBST  Add $100\mathrm{ml}$ of PBS $(10\times)$ to $900\mathrm{ml}$ of double deionized water.   
Add $\mathrm{1ml}$ of Tween 20 and store it at room temperature for 1 year. Blocking buffer, $5\%$ $\mathbf{\Psi}(\mathbf{wt}/\mathbf{vol})$ Dissolve $5\mathrm{g}$ of skim milk in $100\mathrm{ml}$ of PBST.   
Store the buffer at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for 1 week.
hESC/iPSC growth medium  Prepare $\sim500\mathrm{ml}$ of the growth medium. The medium should be used within 2 weeks; however, supplementation with additional FGF2 can be performed after 2 weeks (maximum storage is 4 weeks).
Differentiation basal medium  Prepare $\sim500\mathrm{ml}$ of the differentiation basal medium. Growth factors are supplemented to this medium for the stepwise differentiation process. Store the medium at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 2 months.
BEGM  Prepare the medium according to the manufacturer’s recommenda tion (from BEGM bullet kit). Thaw the frozen supplements provided with the medium at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ overnight before preparing the medium. Store it at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for up to 1 month.
