## (D) Iodide efflux measurement for CFTR activity $\bullet$ TIMING 3 h
(i) Wash apical and basolateral surfaces of cultures with $4~\mathsf{m l}$ of $1\times\mathsf{P B S}$ $(-\mathsf{C a}^{2+}-\mathsf{M g}^{2+})$ twice.   
(ii) Load the basolateral side of cultures with $850~\upmu\upiota$ of iodide solution for $^\textrm{\scriptsize1h}$ at $37^{\circ}\complement$ .   
(iii) After $1\mathfrak{h}$ of incubation, wash the apical and basolateral surfaces with $4~\mathsf{m l}$ of nitrate solution 10 times.   
(iv) Start the discontinuous iodide efflux experiment time course as follows:   
Part 1: add $350~\upmu\upiota$ of nitrate solution and collect the solution into individual wells of a 96-well plate at each minute for 3 min. Part 2: add $350~\upmu\upiota$ of cAMP agonist solution and collect the solution into individual wells of a 96-well plate at each minute for $5\mathrm{\min}$ . (v) Read the iodide concentration of the collected sample solutions using the iodide-sensitive combination microelectrode and the Digidata 1320A data acquisition system with the Clampex 8.1 program.
$\blacktriangle$ CRITICAL STEP Wash the iodide-sensitive combination microelectrode with double deionized water thoroughly between readings.  CRITICAL STEP Make a standard curve for iodide concentration to convert readout to iodide concentration. ?  TROUBLESHOOTING
